-- MONOTONICITY UNDER RENAME — the sibling of `field_owner_no_narrowing/`, and the
-- counterfactual its header used to describe as an accepted fragility.
--
-- That cell's header said, correctly for the compiler of the time:
--
--     "Rename `Wrec` to something sorting before `Dup` and this cell REDDENS, for a
--      reason that has nothing to do with the narrowing it guards."
--
-- This IS that program.  The one variable against `field_owner_no_narrowing/` is the
-- unrelated module's record name — `Wrec` → `Arec` — which moves it ahead of `Dup` in
-- the `sortUniqS`ed owner list for `dx`.  MEASURED on a cold build of the merge base:
-- `Type mismatch: RA vs Arec`, exit 1, on a program whose only edit was renaming a
-- record in a module the projection has nothing to do with.
--
-- Under identity selection the owner-list ORDER stops deciding anything: `mkA.dx`
-- selects the declaration whose `(declaring module, type name)` equals `mkA`'s own
-- head, which no rename of `wmod`'s record can change.  So this cell and
-- `field_owner_no_narrowing/` must now print the SAME value, and that is the property
-- pinned here.
--
-- ⚠️ KEEP BOTH.  The sibling grades that the fallback is not narrowed by import
-- spelling (`import amod.{RA, mkA}` witnesses no constructor for the owner key `Dup`);
-- this one grades that it is not decided by owner-key sort order.  A regression can
-- hit either without the other.
--
-- ⚠️ A WRONG PICK HERE IS A WRONG VALUE, NOT ONLY A DIAGNOSTIC — since #1455's review
-- (finding 2).  `Dup` declares `dpre` before `dx` while `wmod`'s `Arec` declares `dx`
-- first, so the two owners of `dx` disagree on its OFFSET and selecting the wrong one
-- reads `99` instead of `7` on the executed binary.  Before that the record was
-- single-field, both layouts picked index 0, and this cell could only ever have failed
-- as a diagnostic.  Do not collapse it back.
--
-- Hand-derived correct answer, independent of any engine: mkA.dx = 7, mkW.dx = 1,
-- so `8` — the same value its sibling prints, which is the point.
import amod.{RA, mkA}
import wmod.{Arec, mkW}

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (intToString (mkA.dx + mkW.dx))
